Alembic migrations of the backend (async dbapi; env.py builds the URL from DATABASE_*).

Development policy: the application is in development, so there are no incremental
migrations. The whole schema is one hand-written revision, versions/0001_initial.py
(down_revision None): every table, index and constraint in its final shape, the
row-level security policies of the agent role and its column grant on documents. It
has no backfill and no upgrade path from an older database.

On a schema change:

1. Edit the models (src/db/models.py) and edit 0001_initial.py to match them by hand
   (do not autogenerate it, and do not add a new revision).
2. Recreate the database from scratch: `make down-volumes` and then `make up`
   (repository root). The api container runs `specflow migrate` on start.
3. Check it: `make db-upgrade`, then from backend/
   `uv run --env-file ../.env.local alembic check` (the models match the revision) and
   `uv run --env-file ../.env.local alembic current` (prints `0001_initial (head)`).

A database stamped with a revision that no longer exists (for example `0005` from the
old chain) makes `alembic upgrade` fail with "Can't locate revision"; recreate it as in
step 2. downgrade() drops every table the revision created.

migrations/sql/ holds the SQL text the revision reads with its own read_migration_sql
(the revision never imports src/).
